{"text": "The Empty Box.\n\nThe day before the contest, the famous recipe disappeared.\n\nWell, two days before. But it felt like one.\n\nElif was fifteen. Every summer, she worked in her family's small restaurant. It was in Ayvalık, on a street near the sea. In the mornings, Elif cut bread and carried plates. In the evenings, she did the dishes.\n\nThe most famous thing in the restaurant was a cake. It was Aunt Füsun's lemon cake. People came from other towns for it. They always ate one piece and asked for a second.\n\nNobody knew the recipe. Nobody except one old card.\n\nAnd now the card was missing. Who took it? And why?\n\nOn Sunday, there was a summer cake contest in the town square. Every restaurant brought its best cake. This year, Elif wanted to enter with the lemon cake.\n\n\"I'm too old for contests,\" said Aunt Füsun. She laughed. \"You go, Elif. You can make it.\"\n\nAunt Füsun never wrote anything down. She cooked with her hands, not with paper. But there was one card in an old wooden box. It was the recipe for the lemon cake. Everyone in the kitchen knew about that card.\n\nOn Friday morning, Elif opened the box. She wanted to read the card again.\n\nThe box was empty.\n\nElif looked under the box. She looked behind the oven and in every drawer. Nothing.\n\nThen she looked at the kitchen table. There was white flour on it. And in the flour, there were marks from a hand. Somebody touched the box with white hands.\n\n\"Everyone here has white hands,\" Elif thought.\n\nShe went to her room and found an old notebook. On the first page, she wrote three words: \"Find the recipe.\"\n\nUnder them, she wrote: \"Clue one: flour on the table.\"\n\nA real detective needed clues. And a real detective needed suspects.\n\nThat evening, Elif gave Limon his dinner. Limon was the restaurant's cat. He was fat and yellow, like a lemon. In the day, he slept in a basket behind the kitchen door. At night, he always slept on Aunt Füsun's bed.\n\nElif looked into his basket. There was something white under the cat.\n\n\"Move, Limon,\" she said. Limon didn't move. Cats never move when you ask.\n\nElif picked him up slowly. Under him, there was a piece of card. It was half of a card, with old, careful writing.\n\nShe read the first line. It said: \"Lemon Cake.\"", "textSha256": "08003e9154de46024343a187a85dc3feb87e95645b12ad47785dd0cc44324cd5", "voice_id": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "speed": 0.95, "lang": "en", "parts": 1, "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "E", "m", "p", "t", "y", " ", "B", "o", "x", ".", "\n", "\n", "T", "h", "e", " ", "d", "a", "y", " ", "b", "e", "f", "o", "r", "e", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "c", "o", "n", "t", "e", "s", "t", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "a", "m", "o", "u", "s", " ", "r", "e", "c", "i", "p", "e", " ", "d", "i", "s", "a", "p", "p", "e", "a", "r", "e", "d", ".", "\n", "\n", "W", "e", "l", "l", ",", " ", "t", "w", "o", " ", "d", "a", "y", "s", " ", "b", "e", "f", "o", "r", "e", ".", " ", "B", "u", "t", " ", "i", "t", " ", "f", "e", "l", "t", " ", "l", "i", "k", "e", " ", "o", "n", "e", ".", "\n", "\n", "E", "l", "i", "f", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "f", "i", "f", "t", "e", "e", "n", ".", " ", "E", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "s", "u", "m", "m", "e", "r", ",", " ", "s", "h", "e", " ", "w", "o", "r", "k", "e", "d", " ", "i", "n", " ", "h", "e", "r", " ", "f", "a", "m", "i", "l", "y", "'", "s", " ", "s", "m", "a", "l", "l", " ", "r", "e", "s", "t", "a", "u", "r", "a", "n", "t", ".", " ", "I", "t", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "i", "n", " ", "A", "y", "v", "a", "l", "ı", "k", ",", " ", "o", "n", " ", "a", " ", "s", "t", "r", "e", "e", "t", " ", "n", "e", "a", "r", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "e", "a", ".", " ", "I", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "m", "o", "r", "n", "i", "n", "g", "s", ",", " ", "E", "l", "i", "f", " ", "c", "u", "t", " ", "b", "r", "e", "a", "d", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "c", "a", "r", "r", "i", "e", "d", " ", "p", "l", "a", "t", "e", "s", ".", " ", "I", "n"